---
export const prerender = true;

import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ServiceLayout from '../../components/service/ServiceLayout.astro';
import TrackingFlow from '../../components/TrackingFlow.astro';
import { serviceBySlug } from '../../config/services';

const service = serviceBySlug('conversion-tracking')!;
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How is this different from the GA4 implementation service?',
    a: 'Analytics implementation is about building the collection layer: properties, tags, configuration. Conversion tracking and behaviour analytics is about the questions: which conversions matter, which paths to trace, which drop-offs to investigate, and what the patterns mean for decisions.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you record our users or access private data?',
    a: 'No. Behaviour work uses aggregated analytics, and if session replay tools are involved we work inside accounts you own, under your consent configuration. The demonstration on this page is simulated and collects nothing.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What if our tracking is currently broken?',
    a: 'That is a normal starting point. Repairs are scoped first: identify what is wrong, fix the collection, then rebuild the analysis on top of data you can trust.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What formats do findings come in?',
    a: 'Funnel views, annotated journey maps, event timelines and a written analysis linking each observation to a suggested next step. Everything is designed to be read by non-analysts.',
  },
];
---

<Base title={service.metaTitle} description={service.metaDescription} canonicalPath={service.path}>
  <ServiceLayout
    service={service}
    lede="Follow the path from first visit to meaningful action: reliable conversion tracking, funnels and behaviour analysis that show where the journey loses people and what to investigate next."
    artAlt="Soft coral and amber topography relief on a white surface with a light trail and glowing markers"
    faqs={faqs}
    visualTone="tone-paper"
    problemTitle="Totals tell you what. Journeys tell you where."
    problemLead="A conversion rate that dropped this month is a symptom. The useful work starts when you can see the steps people actually took."
    deliverablesTitle="Tracking and behaviour deliverables"
    deliverablesLead="From conversion definitions to annotated journey analysis, everything arrives readable."
    processTitle="How an analysis engagement runs"
    processVariant="rail"
    scopeTitle="What conversion tracking includes"
  >
    <Fragment slot="visual">
      <TrackingFlow />
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="problem">
      <p>
        A single number cannot explain itself. Conversion rate fell from 3.1% to 2.6%? That
        could be traffic quality, a broken checkout step, a seasonal shift, a tracking change or
        a price increase. <strong>Without the journey, you are guessing between them.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        Conversion tracking and behaviour analytics connects the dots: which events fired, which
        steps people completed, where they stalled, and which drop-off patterns repeat across
        segments. It turns &ldquo;something changed&rdquo; into &ldquo;here is the step, here
        is the segment, here is what to look at.&rdquo;
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Privacy by design:</strong> analysis works on aggregated behaviour and the data
        your own tools already collect under your consent settings. Nothing on this site
        records real visitors, and no client data is accessed outside agreed accounts and
        agreed scope.
      </div>
      <p>
        The output is not a pile of charts. It is a short list of moments worth acting on, each
        with the evidence that put it there.
      </p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="deliverables">
      <ul class="deliver-grid">
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Conversion map</h3>
            <p>Every meaningful action defined once: what counts, what does not and why.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Funnel definitions</h3>
            <p>Step sequences written to match how people really move, including edge paths.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Drop-off analysis</h3>
            <p>Where people leave, segmented by source, device and intent where data allows.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">04</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Journey annotations</h3>
            <p>Marked up paths linking behaviour to interface moments, ready for a designer or developer.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">05</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Event timeline</h3>
            <p>Sequence analysis: what happened before the drop, not just where it happened.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">06</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Investigation list</h3>
            <p>A ranked set of moments to verify, test or fix, with the supporting evidence attached.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="extra">
      <section class="section-sm sv-extra" aria-labelledby="sv-funnel-title" style={`--accent:${service.accent}; --soft:${service.accentSoft};`}>
        <div class="container-x">
          <header class="extra-head">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal="fade">Example output</p>
              <h2 class="display-md" id="sv-funnel-title" data-reveal>Funnel with drop-off signals</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="extra-note" data-reveal="fade">
              Illustrative figures. Real analyses use your data and show the segments that
              behave differently from each other.
            </p>
          </header>
          <div class="funnel-demo" data-reveal="fade">
            <div class="fd-row">
              <span class="fd-label">Product viewed</span>
              <span class="fd-bar"><i style="width:100%"></i></span>
              <span class="fd-val">100%</span>
            </div>
            <div class="fd-row">
              <span class="fd-label">Size or variant chosen</span>
              <span class="fd-bar"><i style="width:71%"></i></span>
              <span class="fd-val">71%</span>
              <span class="fd-flag">-29% step loss</span>
            </div>
            <div class="fd-row">
              <span class="fd-label">Added to cart</span>
              <span class="fd-bar"><i style="width:48%"></i></span>
              <span class="fd-val">48%</span>
            </div>
            <div class="fd-row">
              <span class="fd-label">Checkout started</span>
              <span class="fd-bar"><i style="width:31%"></i></span>
              <span class="fd-val">31%</span>
              <span class="fd-flag">-17% step loss</span>
            </div>
            <div class="fd-row">
              <span class="fd-label">Purchase completed</span>
              <span class="fd-bar fd-last"><i style="width:19%"></i></span>
              <span class="fd-val">19%</span>
            </div>
            <p class="fd-note">
              Two steps carry most of the loss. That is where the investigation starts, and
              where an experiment would be cheaper than a redesign.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="process">
      <ol class="p-rail">
        <li>
          <span class="p-num">STEP 01</span>
          <h3>Define</h3>
          <p>Agree the conversions and journeys that matter to the business, in plain language, before touching a tool.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="p-num">STEP 02</span>
          <h3>Verify</h3>
          <p>Check that the tracking behind each step is accurate: firing rules, parameters, duplicates, consent.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="p-num">STEP 03</span>
          <h3>Trace</h3>
          <p>Build funnel and journey views, then walk through them segment by segment to find real patterns.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="p-num">STEP 04</span>
          <h3>Report</h3>
          <p>Deliver findings as annotated journeys and an investigation list, then decide what to test or fix first.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="scope">
      <ul>
        <li>Includes conversion definitions, funnel construction, drop-off analysis and written findings.</li>
        <li>Includes repair of broken or untrusted tracking where it blocks the analysis.</li>
        <li>Uses aggregated data from tools you own; no recording of individual visitors is performed by CROLANE.</li>
        <li>Live heatmaps or replay platforms, if you want them, are implemented in your own accounts under your consent policy.</li>
        <li>The on-page journey demonstration is simulated sample data and collects nothing.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Recommendations are tied to evidence you can inspect. If the data cannot support a
        conclusion, the report will say that instead of filling the gap with a story.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </ServiceLayout>
</Base>

<style>
  .sv-extra {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color-paper), #fdeee6);
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 7%, transparent);
  }

  .extra-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .extra-head > div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .extra-note {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-3);
    max-width: 26rem;
  }

  .funnel-demo {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 10%, transparent);
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: clamp(1.3rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
    max-width: 52rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .fd-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 12rem minmax(0, 1fr) 3rem;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .fd-label {
    font-size: 0.87rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
  }

  .fd-bar {
    height: 26px;
    border-radius: 7px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 7%, transparent);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .fd-bar i {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff), var(--accent));
    border-radius: inherit;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .fd-last i {
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-emerald) 60%, #fff), var(--color-emerald));
  }

  .fd-val {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-align: right;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fd-flag {
    position: absolute;
    right: 3.8rem;
    top: -0.55rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-coral) 12%, #fff);
    color: var(--color-coral);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-coral) 40%, transparent);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.45rem;
  }

  .fd-note {
    font-size: 0.87rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    border-top: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 14%, transparent);
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: 0.3rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .fd-row {
      grid-template-columns: 8.5rem minmax(0, 1fr) 2.6rem;
      gap: 0.6rem;
    }

    .fd-flag {
      position: static;
      grid-column: 2 / -1;
      justify-self: start;
      margin-top: -0.4rem;
    }
  }
</style>
